    "report": "Messaging and Notifications no longer read the machine's time. Every time they decide or record now comes from the application's clock, passed in from the composition root. The work is committed as `dc03b30` on `main`, the current branch. I did not push.\n\n**What changed**\n- **Messaging domain:** `Conversation.start` (`sentAt`), `send` and `report` take the time as a required parameter. The `new Date()` fallbacks are gone.\n- **Messaging application:** the start, send and report handlers all take the clock with no default. The report handler did not have one before, so I added it. `messagingWiring` takes the clock with no default too.\n- **Notifications domain:** `NoticeWindow.admit`, `MessageNoticeOwing.owe` and `Notice.accept` take the time as a required parameter.\n- **Notifications application:** `MessageSentIntegrationEventHandler` and `NoticeDelivery` take the clock. `notificationsWiring` now takes `clock` after `languages`, and `createApplication` passes the application's clock.\n\n**Verification**\n- Typecheck, ESLint, `check:conventions` and `format:check` are all clean.\n- Unit tests: 155 suites, 1049 tests pass.\n- Full e2e: 114 suites, 607 tests pass.\n- No non-spec file in Messaging or Notifications still reads `new Date()` or `Date.now()`.\n\n**Choices I made**\n- **Specs:** about 45 spec call sites relied on the defaults. I gave each a fixed instant (`2026-03-01T10:00:00Z`), so each test keeps the same meaning. I did not change any assertion.\n- **Clock read once per reaction:** `MessageSentIntegrationEventHandler` reads the clock once per event, before its conflict-retry loop, so every retry decides at the same instant.\n- **Left as is:** `messageNoticeWindowSeconds = 900` is a configuration default, not a machine-time read. `messageClock.routes.e2e.spec.ts` still reads `Date.now()`, but only to check that the clock applies the offset.\n\n**Branch:** The repo's guidance says to branch off a default branch before committing. You asked for the current branch, so I committed on `main`. If you want it on a separate branch, that's a quick move.",
